From: piano bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] BootShim: describe the whole image and a zero text offset

piano's ABL reads the ARM64 image header the way the ARM64 specification
defines it:

- image_size must describe the whole image (the shim plus the firmware
  volume). Upstream writes FD_SIZE alone, which is only the volume.
- text_offset is a displacement from the load address, not an absolute
  address. Upstream writes FD_BASE there, so an ABL that computes
  load + text_offset lands far outside the reservation, and the tablet
  drops straight back to fastboot (observed: fastboot boot returns
  "Booting OKAY" and nothing else happens).

The stock piano kernel reports text_offset 0x0, and the shim's copy loop
reads FD_BASE from a literal pool that this patch leaves alone.

--- a/BootShim/BootShim.S
+++ b/BootShim/BootShim.S
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ _StackBase:
-  .quad FD_BASE         /* Text Offset */
+  .quad 0               /* Text Offset: displacement, not an address */
 
 _StackSize:
-  .quad FD_SIZE         /* Image Size */
+  .quad FD_SIZE + _Payload - _Head   /* Image Size: shim plus volume */
   .quad 0               /* Flags */
   .quad 0               /* Reserved */
   .quad 0               /* Reserved */
